"The postoperative pathology revealed a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological stage pT3a. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins, absence of seminal vesicle invasion, and absence of lymphovascular invasion. The nodal status is pNx, meaning no nodes were removed, which widens uncertainty regarding nodal involvement as pNx does not establish pN0 disease. The preoperative PSA was 6.9. The documented surgical findings are reassuring regarding local control. Countervailing factors include the pNx status, which limits staging, and the preoperative PSA level. Postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory are needed to assess biochemical recurrence. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory would significantly revise the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 54.81 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 35.62–73.99 months; its coverage has not been validated."
